  "solution": {
    "text": "The enol of beta-dicarbonyl compounds are more stable because of conjugation and intramolecular H-bonding. Thus, the order of stability is,<br /><br /><math> <mrow>  <munder>   <mrow>    <msub>     <mrow>      <mtext>CH</mtext>     </mrow>     <mn>3</mn>    </msub>    <mo>&#x2212;</mo><mover>     <mrow>      <mover>       <mtext>C</mtext>       <mo>&#x007C;</mo>      </mover>      <mo>=</mo>     </mrow>     <mrow>      <mtext>OH</mtext>     </mrow>    </mover>    <mtext>CH</mtext><mo>&#x2212;</mo><mover>     <mrow>      <mover>       <mtext>C</mtext>       <mrow>        <mo>&#x007C;</mo><mo>&#x007C;</mo>       </mrow>      </mover>           </mrow>     <mtext>O</mtext>    </mover>    <mo>&#x2212;</mo><msub>     <mrow>      <mtext>CH</mtext>     </mrow>     <mn>3</mn>    </msub>       </mrow>   <mrow>    <mtext>III</mtext>   </mrow>  </munder>  <mo>&#x003E;</mo><munder>   <mrow>    <msub>     <mrow>      <mtext>CH</mtext>     </mrow>     <mn>3</mn>    </msub>    <mo>&#x2212;</mo><mtext>CO</mtext><mo>&#x2212;</mo><msub>     <mrow>      <mtext>CH</mtext>     </mrow>     <mn>2</mn>    </msub>    <mo>&#x2212;</mo><mtext>CO</mtext><mo>&#x2212;</mo><msub>     <mrow>      <mtext>CH</mtext>     </mrow>     <mn>3</mn>    </msub>       </mrow>   <mrow>    <mtext>II</mtext>   </mrow>  </munder>  <mo>&#x003E;</mo><munder>   <mrow>    <msub>     <mrow>      <mtext>CH</mtext>     </mrow>     <mn>2</mn>    </msub>    <mo>=</mo><mtext>C</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo>     <mrow>      <mtext>OH</mtext>     </mrow>    <mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>&#x2212;</mo><msub>     <mrow>      <mtext>CH</mtext>     </mrow>     <mn>2</mn>    </msub>    <mo>&#x2212;</mo><mtext>CO</mtext><mo>&#x2212;</mo><msub>     <mrow>      <mtext>CH</mtext>     </mrow>     <mn>3</mn>    </msub>       </mrow>   <mtext>I</mtext>  </munder>   </mrow></math><br /><br />I is less stable as (=) bond is not in conjugation with carbonly group.<br /><br />III is most stable due to conjugation of (=) bond and intramolecular hydrogen bonding."
